  "segments": [
    {
      "sentence_index": 1,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "John Stuart Mill's fear that the notes of the piano might be used up and tunes give out is as nothing to mine that a time must come when there will be no more whimsical literature in the old book shops for these eyes to alight upon.",
      "output_sha256": "cfa3df6018eee9f26ead8659aab2e1b558508a967d9e98e81916fc3c7aed8bb9",
      "alignment_unit_index": 1,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 1,
      "source_human_sha256": "cfa3df6018eee9f26ead8659aab2e1b558508a967d9e98e81916fc3c7aed8bb9",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 2,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Meanwhile, to renew my confidence, a friend sends me \"The Compleat English Physician, or The Druggist's Shop Opened (the like not hitherto extant)\" by William Salmon, who dates his preface \"From my house at the Blew Ball by the Ditch-side near Holborn Bridge, London, May 5, 1693.\"",
      "output_sha256": "b5b4339575f0db4c9e2c7ec763cd2cbc6cbc8aec5c9f21e4c98cab5f4786e48e",
      "alignment_unit_index": 2,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 2,
      "source_human_sha256": "b5b4339575f0db4c9e2c7ec763cd2cbc6cbc8aec5c9f21e4c98cab5f4786e48e",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 3,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "In this exhaustive work the whole of creation, animal, vegetable, and mineral, is levied upon for cures for human ills, any of which are, in the dedication, offered by the author to the Most Serene and Illustrious Princess Mary II., if she feels herself to be in need of physic and will lay her commands upon him.",
      "output_sha256": "382180972ed5332a780afc4c2e1d1e0d823e477fd028e0a6999a5db2b06c8d08",
      "alignment_unit_index": 3,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 3,
      "source_human_sha256": "382180972ed5332a780afc4c2e1d1e0d823e477fd028e0a6999a5db2b06c8d08",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 4,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "According to \"The Dictionary of National Biography,\" which, however, does not mention this particular book, William Salmon was born in 1644, and was educated by a mountebank.",
      "output_sha256": "acebd0fc26a72857397aa0e0fe334afb02e2e190e2fddb077466f570e3d3583a",
      "alignment_unit_index": 4,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 4,
      "source_human_sha256": "acebd0fc26a72857397aa0e0fe334afb02e2e190e2fddb077466f570e3d3583a",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 5,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "After a certain amount of travel, he settled in London as an irregular practitioner, with pills for everything and horoscopes to boot.",
      "output_sha256": "0dce8d47997a84c6e61efe9198691a26261f6be8aeac5d1fd8ddcfbcf74ceb54",
      "alignment_unit_index": 5,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 5,
      "source_human_sha256": "0dce8d47997a84c6e61efe9198691a26261f6be8aeac5d1fd8ddcfbcf74ceb54",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 6,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "There was speculation during his lifetime that he may not have been the original source of the extensive knowledge reflected in his numerous volumes, but rather an amanuensis.",
      "output_sha256": "566f48d4361d1f65c50ef48a06f562ceb1ba0ea3d73456bc674b8b1f78b9bb38",
      "alignment_unit_index": 6,
      "alignment_score": 0.550917,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        6
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "e1e348d82820806e554d24f7769cc672f5f804af14a07e90afda0b7b7b146821"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 6,
      "source_ai_sha256": "566f48d4361d1f65c50ef48a06f562ceb1ba0ea3d73456bc674b8b1f78b9bb38",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        6,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 7,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The \"Dictionary\" corroborates this theory; however, in the preface to \"The Compleat English Physician,\" Salmon vehemently defends himself against one critic, whom he describes as \"the nasty author of an impertinent and scurrilous pamphlet,\" asserting that he has accumulated thirty years of practical pharmacy experience.",
      "output_sha256": "441a1e3dad5722ef6e3a31c1d7b736ace4c70c33227929c5c27da70bb141d7dd",
      "alignment_unit_index": 6,
      "alignment_score": 0.550917,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        6
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "e1e348d82820806e554d24f7769cc672f5f804af14a07e90afda0b7b7b146821"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 7,
      "source_ai_sha256": "441a1e3dad5722ef6e3a31c1d7b736ace4c70c33227929c5c27da70bb141d7dd",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        6,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 8,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "Yet, it seems improbable that even three decades of diligent work could suffice to gather the vast array of insights found within this remarkable tome.",
      "output_sha256": "8e1bc2920dd1b4a6376a423fe45efe0675c144499148bb7ccf2fc66f8b90d40d",
      "alignment_unit_index": 7,
      "alignment_score": 0.304848,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        7
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "9787360b884dc6ca700d0cb1a5d912adf69949f99a6c94f83aec96f14a5564d4"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 8,
      "source_ai_sha256": "8e1bc2920dd1b4a6376a423fe45efe0675c144499148bb7ccf2fc66f8b90d40d",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 9,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Although it is exclusively medical, Salmon incidentally hits upon as deadly a formula for anti-social satire as could be imagined, beyond even Swift.",
      "output_sha256": "4390fb9fd7e06683c15e4e4f182f9bb3674f4c7d3635aaf59f7067d947b3eb86",
      "alignment_unit_index": 8,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 8,
      "source_human_sha256": "4390fb9fd7e06683c15e4e4f182f9bb3674f4c7d3635aaf59f7067d947b3eb86",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 10,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "Not all the bitterness found in \"Gulliver's Travels\" can equal the effect of this empiric's unassuming classification of humanity alongside the animal kingdom.",
      "output_sha256": "825ba686eff493e14c70c45a79b7dc64dabd18af69cc39569b8685e72d96abf5",
      "alignment_unit_index": 9,
      "alignment_score": 0.458597,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        9
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "af1c106a9f3541263755ab8fad44e800514046651338c0dc0fe22bae13d105c7"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 10,
      "source_ai_sha256": "825ba686eff493e14c70c45a79b7dc64dabd18af69cc39569b8685e72d96abf5",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 11,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "In Book V, titled \"Of Man and Beasts,\" he begins with the statement: \"Chapter 1.",
      "output_sha256": "374ef60dae36ad24f0be626494a280620817b364d06b7732aa755911e9cd5daa",
      "alignment_unit_index": 10,
      "alignment_score": 0.699743,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        10
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "fe699e8f530a1f457c5a7c86a9eff0771daef291b6c5bd706b027f64929d401a"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 11,
      "source_ai_sha256": "374ef60dae36ad24f0be626494a280620817b364d06b7732aa755911e9cd5daa",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 12,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Homo, Man & Woman....",
      "output_sha256": "9da2694696ef790483d611770b1c5fbf2770c95ca1e741f9ee78f773dc5044dc",
      "alignment_unit_index": 11,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 11,
      "source_human_sha256": "9da2694696ef790483d611770b1c5fbf2770c95ca1e741f9ee78f773dc5044dc",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 13,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "They are the general inhabitants of the Universal Globe of the Earth and their food is made of Grain, Pulse, Fruits, Flowers, Roots, Herbs, and the flesh of Beasts, Fowl, Fishes, Insects, etc.\" Salmon then goes on to enumerate the maladies that the various parts of man (and woman) are good for.",
      "output_sha256": "4b12f5713ae093a9cf3b78ff3847817482adf592315f57b6ae577f039123a28e",
      "alignment_unit_index": 12,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 12,
      "source_human_sha256": "4b12f5713ae093a9cf3b78ff3847817482adf592315f57b6ae577f039123a28e",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 14,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "His hair, converted to ashes and powdered, will cure the Green Sickness and other disorders too elementary to name.",
      "output_sha256": "91424635769af849cf926ac3014563fbaa353a6573703738c8b0708fd88a5f78",
      "alignment_unit_index": 13,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 13,
      "source_human_sha256": "91424635769af849cf926ac3014563fbaa353a6573703738c8b0708fd88a5f78",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 15,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Made into an oil it will ease pains caused by a cold and cause new hair to grow on bald places.",
      "output_sha256": "d134e19eb5b1c314e015142f5ce385b7aa9212ba62aeacef0e16b2e50a07723b",
      "alignment_unit_index": 14,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 14,
      "source_human_sha256": "d134e19eb5b1c314e015142f5ce385b7aa9212ba62aeacef0e16b2e50a07723b",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 16,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The rest of the human body, whether in the form of powder, volatile oil, spirit, essence, salt, magistry, or balsam, is similarly beneficial for a myriad of ailments.",
      "output_sha256": "df49e1c6db5eb65b7fd6127ae101086625570d1ebc70690e52bc507a7d2f5b3a",
      "alignment_unit_index": 15,
      "alignment_score": 0.408521,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        15
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "736b9bab6d14093801903dd53d29ece50cf9cfc867f516d41b63218b98c6760c"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 16,
      "source_ai_sha256": "df49e1c6db5eb65b7fd6127ae101086625570d1ebc70690e52bc507a7d2f5b3a",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 17,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "It is an ironical and exasperating thought that we carry about in our bodies the cures for all the ills that those bodies suffer from.",
      "output_sha256": "d7dca52d3366f95f19dcb5a4792bf78fcca50a4b5f59bee4b9e8e2c2e820d03d",
      "alignment_unit_index": 16,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 16,
      "source_human_sha256": "d7dca52d3366f95f19dcb5a4792bf78fcca50a4b5f59bee4b9e8e2c2e820d03d",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 18,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "In most of the sciences the professors of the day know more than their predecessors of yesterday.",
      "output_sha256": "2f0954e8a4643826986769d669a232e2db37c49ab429e580f6708e4f6144f06d",
      "alignment_unit_index": 17,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 17,
      "source_human_sha256": "2f0954e8a4643826986769d669a232e2db37c49ab429e580f6708e4f6144f06d",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 19,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Knowledge accumulates.",
      "output_sha256": "1172bd7a615a217866a5edc18cec438df1dc6f7612a7b87a90a610c30d6b2311",
      "alignment_unit_index": 18,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 18,
      "source_human_sha256": "1172bd7a615a217866a5edc18cec438df1dc6f7612a7b87a90a610c30d6b2311",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 20,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "But, after dipping into Salmon's twelve-hundred pages, one sighs with relief that the healing art has, since 1693, become comparatively so simple; and when next sending for a doctor we shall thank God for his modern incompleatness.",
      "output_sha256": "716f64dbcb04624c0ec834d4398b6478822d1df737f6bdbed2e0b1fc8f242675",
      "alignment_unit_index": 19,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 19,
      "source_human_sha256": "716f64dbcb04624c0ec834d4398b6478822d1df737f6bdbed2e0b1fc8f242675",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 21,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "For in Salmon's day, in the pride of compleation, the medical man might have dosed us with our nearest dead neighbour.",
      "output_sha256": "f70418ca9e02cb8f55a68be99663059b6415ff27b1d64ef017bfbffcc8b95408",
      "alignment_unit_index": 20,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 20,
      "source_human_sha256": "f70418ca9e02cb8f55a68be99663059b6415ff27b1d64ef017bfbffcc8b95408",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 22,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Having finished the examination of man as a treasury of restoratives, Salmon passes on to Alces, the Elk; Antilopus, the Antelope; and Asinus, the Ass.",
      "output_sha256": "6e64de6e7c15db51e72ae1e9cfbb3af512307a2084ffb178912eb6bfb4b4b4f8",
      "alignment_unit_index": 21,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 21,
      "source_human_sha256": "6e64de6e7c15db51e72ae1e9cfbb3af512307a2084ffb178912eb6bfb4b4b4f8",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 23,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "All the beasts are therapeutically useful to man, but few more so than Asinus, the Ass.",
      "output_sha256": "45e478fbe6ba2b11817ea12574c804e5099e972de039e4e83d29c7e457c4294e",
      "alignment_unit_index": 22,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 22,
      "source_human_sha256": "45e478fbe6ba2b11817ea12574c804e5099e972de039e4e83d29c7e457c4294e",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 24,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "While a living donkey has its merits, it pales in comparison to the extensive benefits derived from a deceased donkey transformed into medicinal compounds.",
      "output_sha256": "15fa22bc3db168c5c28cf4267d8394e8dc6cf1eab9009247fcad3b0627ca4af6",
      "alignment_unit_index": 23,
      "alignment_score": 0.3525,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        23
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "89ba92a5902fb31db0e620c7957b988fdf45fef95177a085d78600296c36f8af"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 25,
      "source_ai_sha256": "15fa22bc3db168c5c28cf4267d8394e8dc6cf1eab9009247fcad3b0627ca4af6",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        25
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 25,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Equus, the Horse; Capra, the Goat; and Cercopithecus, the Monkey, are also each a well-stocked chemist's shop.",
      "output_sha256": "0bcbe22ac472ef64c256e204b473de221e8cd20ed0572bdabae3d22ed06fd9d3",
      "alignment_unit_index": 24,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 24,
      "source_human_sha256": "0bcbe22ac472ef64c256e204b473de221e8cd20ed0572bdabae3d22ed06fd9d3",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 26,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "Indeed, anything that moves, whether on two legs or four, yields potent elixirs, yet it is the inclusion of humanity in this mix that is jarring.",
      "output_sha256": "a0edfdfa5ac609ae5c19527cb359797f9b3577e4a808dff2feb74705310ae8e8",
      "alignment_unit_index": 25,
      "alignment_score": 0.417423,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        25
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "2c945885b5f7025fd916089d38347e7a63d883b52b8df24d7f214fed64f603fa"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 27,
      "source_ai_sha256": "a0edfdfa5ac609ae5c19527cb359797f9b3577e4a808dff2feb74705310ae8e8",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        27
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 27,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "It seems appropriate for the Lord of Creation to extract remedies from his soulless inferiors, but to do so from himself is a disheartening notion.",
      "output_sha256": "f7c858b5081bc0c19e21d9bcb32f72aa6d01b0f594509046955a3aece0df3a50",
      "alignment_unit_index": 26,
      "alignment_score": 0.501472,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "3e969e117a4bedf96edac78690191037dada4445cb5a173a7f87ae92b540314d",
        "779c57ed091aa383f6ec803c68e0a3d393b679ba602fda5cf12ac5ee59ce26fd"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 28,
      "source_ai_sha256": "f7c858b5081bc0c19e21d9bcb32f72aa6d01b0f594509046955a3aece0df3a50",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        28
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 28,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The avian world also contributes to this pharmacopoeia.",
      "output_sha256": "add0dce6bbbc591d61fa8aab3de59760d452b7dd9c7758a14644a56922e06c52",
      "alignment_unit_index": 27,
      "alignment_score": 0.264286,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        28
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "3a60e4bd3e21c8c1e1ff7c7bcc3f85d81f6a6045c8d372e8693b88f39e39fbf5"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 29,
      "source_ai_sha256": "add0dce6bbbc591d61fa8aab3de59760d452b7dd9c7758a14644a56922e06c52",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        29
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 29,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Thus: the flesh of Alauda, the Lark, will ease the cholick: a thing to remember at Ye Old Cheshire Cheese.",
      "output_sha256": "19a4cdd2a4455defa360e807b5f76eb0ebb4f7131c1207b0b07ce58bc8160ae8",
      "alignment_unit_index": 28,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 29,
      "source_human_sha256": "19a4cdd2a4455defa360e807b5f76eb0ebb4f7131c1207b0b07ce58bc8160ae8",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 30,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Alcedo, the Kingfisher, reduced to powder and mixed with powder made from a man's skull, and a little salt of amber, is excellent against the epilepsy.",
      "output_sha256": "d74551a2d0beea221abbcb7986bc40670de1d6c8b73ffd886f532fb2e7d71a57",
      "alignment_unit_index": 29,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 30,
      "source_human_sha256": "d74551a2d0beea221abbcb7986bc40670de1d6c8b73ffd886f532fb2e7d71a57",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 31,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "A number of swallows beaten to pieces in a mortar (terrible thought!) produce a residuum that will prevent the falling sickness.",
      "output_sha256": "5f5143a79d14bbe25812b474993270e97677a02302b05c6adc7f3a84389aaa63",
      "alignment_unit_index": 30,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 31,
      "source_human_sha256": "5f5143a79d14bbe25812b474993270e97677a02302b05c6adc7f3a84389aaa63",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 32,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "For restoring a lost memory the heart of Hirundo, the Swallow, to which the filings of a man's skull (Mr. Pelman's for choice?) and dried peony roots are added, is sovran.",
      "output_sha256": "001d6ec713c4366df172ce271806e8798148751046ec35c7b3173ace6570b3db",
      "alignment_unit_index": 31,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 32,
      "source_human_sha256": "001d6ec713c4366df172ce271806e8798148751046ec35c7b3173ace6570b3db",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 33,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Even the nest of Hirundo, the Swallow, is of use; made into a cataplasm it not only eases a quinsie, but will cure the bite of a serpent.",
      "output_sha256": "72b22444233118e6d9873b13072cb519825b7d80a079ccf413109031a433ddbe",
      "alignment_unit_index": 32,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 33,
      "source_human_sha256": "72b22444233118e6d9873b13072cb519825b7d80a079ccf413109031a433ddbe",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 34,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Nor are the fragile systems of Rubecula, the Robin Red-breast, and Regulus, the Wren (shade of Blake!), without medicinal utility.",
      "output_sha256": "40865195e0c003aa7ce48c3e36b3cc21c4006a9fd07c8afce74c19d30fa58562",
      "alignment_unit_index": 33,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 34,
      "source_human_sha256": "40865195e0c003aa7ce48c3e36b3cc21c4006a9fd07c8afce74c19d30fa58562",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 35,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The flesh of Lucinia, the Nightingale, is said to help those suffering from consumption, while its gall mixed with honey creates an excellent eye wash.",
      "output_sha256": "0af182ea95915a839f19147eca47b423fc4c2ea2f42c80f732b6f47301e148f6",
      "alignment_unit_index": 34,
      "alignment_score": 0.494169,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        35
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "3d54df10a0eb3066e11c40f9e8c7db75c7354da66e1b2371c921b436c13e1718"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 36,
      "source_ai_sha256": "0af182ea95915a839f19147eca47b423fc4c2ea2f42c80f732b6f47301e148f6",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        36,
        37
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 36,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "However, it seems unjust that songbirds should be subjected to such exploitation.",
      "output_sha256": "900660e046ba2af862ea90f85132417cadd53b71101331c0842cf00536e12b3e",
      "alignment_unit_index": 34,
      "alignment_score": 0.494169,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        35
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "3d54df10a0eb3066e11c40f9e8c7db75c7354da66e1b2371c921b436c13e1718"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 37,
      "source_ai_sha256": "900660e046ba2af862ea90f85132417cadd53b71101331c0842cf00536e12b3e",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        36,
        37
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 37,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "\"Yet\" (you say) \"if the nightingale cures consumption, it might have cured Keats.\"",
      "output_sha256": "ac9992fe2b4940708b06a8db93893f47047e8c2c92e260cd4e894d28b6d7df99",
      "alignment_unit_index": 35,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 36,
      "source_human_sha256": "ac9992fe2b4940708b06a8db93893f47047e8c2c92e260cd4e894d28b6d7df99",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 38,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "True, but had Keats accepted that remedy he would not have been Keats.",
      "output_sha256": "ee924f64f5900536820a0723041122615ae9808179f4c0e4a351e492b893a568",
      "alignment_unit_index": 36,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 37,
      "source_human_sha256": "ee924f64f5900536820a0723041122615ae9808179f4c0e4a351e492b893a568",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 39,
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "In his discussion of Lucinia, the Nightingale, Salmon makes an observation—entirely unnecessary—that sets him apart among authors.",
      "output_sha256": "f93378c183e9a31f479cc35721cd57c8e166eab7b409dc15e6ab5befad085dbb",
      "alignment_unit_index": 37,
      "alignment_score": 0.488075,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        38
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "30b9ff2880d6812f9a4b68b823d03fa3067de18b623029472d996c793ba7fb4f"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 40,
      "source_ai_sha256": "f93378c183e9a31f479cc35721cd57c8e166eab7b409dc15e6ab5befad085dbb",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 40,
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "He perpetrates a curiosity of literature: the most unpoetical thing ever written.",
      "output_sha256": "8b3e9e98819242f41a1932ceced3ff2f036f7d9233e3ba373270fd393f04e59c",
      "alignment_unit_index": 38,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 39,
      "source_human_sha256": "8b3e9e98819242f41a1932ceced3ff2f036f7d9233e3ba373270fd393f04e59c",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 41,
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "While the phrase \"A Mr. Wilkinson, a clergyman,\" may stand as the most uninspired line in poetry, the assertion that Lucinia, the Nightingale, \"grows fat in autumn,\" completely erases the enchantment associated with this iconic bird.",
      "output_sha256": "8ffe16c7af68e40d9c907d9fba5fdc787d3d39da8849969fcb85469f8cd0097a",
      "alignment_unit_index": 39,
      "alignment_score": 0.536496,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        40
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "bf1629eda7c0862c1007053916d5429c334ea7b1f581e3e51b6408ebffcdb2f4"
      ],
